            "id": "0000021",
            "elType": "widget",
            "widgetType": "heading",
            "settings": {
              "title": "Good work begins<br>with a shared picture.",
              "header_size": "h1",
              "_css_classes": ""
            },
            "elements": []
          },
          {
            "id": "0000022",
            "elType": "widget",
            "widgetType": "text-editor",
            "settings": {
              "editor": "<p class=\"north-intro\">Northline is fictional. Its website shows how clear service content and an editable WordPress build can make a small-business enquiry easier.</p><h2>Understand before promising</h2><p>Describe the task plainly. Identify what is included, what needs checking and when specialist input is necessary.</p><h2>Keep the handover useful</h2><p>Record the agreed work and explain any next steps. The same principle applies to this website: straightforward editing, documented setup and visible limitations.</p>"
            },
            "elements": []
          },
          {
            "id": "0000023",
            "elType": "widget",
            "widgetType": "html",
            "settings": {
              "html": "<div class=\"north-faq\"><details><summary>Can I book a real job?</summary><p>No. This is a website demonstration. No messages or bookings are sent.</p></details><details><summary>Can the content be edited?</summary><p>Yes. The page headings, text and buttons are native Elementor widgets. The shared header and styling belong to the child theme.</p></details></div>"
            },
            "elements": []
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
